    "label": "2",
    "prompt": "A sentence has 27 English words. Prove that at least two words start with the same letter.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "There are 26 possible initial letters and 27 words, so the pigeonhole principle guarantees that at least two words start with the same letter.",
      "worked": "Label 26 holes with the letters of the English alphabet. Place each of the 27 words into the hole corresponding to its first letter. Since there are 27 words and only 26 holes, the pigeonhole principle guarantees that some hole contains at least two words. These words start with the same letter.",
